caption: Exceeding Capacity
technology-rule: exceeding-capacity

Whenever a new dose raises the character above Chem Capacity, make an Overdose roll:

Overdose Roll = HT + Highest Relevant Physical Talent - Current Excess - Previous Dissolution or Overdose Rolls

Where:

Current Excess is the number of uncleared chems above Chem Capacity.

Previous Rolls is the number of Dissolution or Overdose rolls made in the previous 25 hours.

The penalty increases with every additional unsafe dose.

Each chem records an Overdose Effect:

Coma

Heart Attack

Both

Failure causes the listed condition.

A critical failure, or failure while already suffering the listed condition, causes death.

Luck and ordinary Resistance do not aid Overdose rolls unless they have the Cosmic modifier.

If the character reaches twice their normal Chem Capacity, they die immediately, subject to normal GM judgment concerning involuntary drugging.
